{{!
    @template block_lp/competencies_to_review_page

    The competencies waiting for review, overridden by Dimensions.

    Mirrors block_lp/competencies_to_review_page of Moodle 5.3 (2026100500), blocks/lp/templates/competencies_to_review_page.mustache.
    Re-diff it against that file on every core upgrade. The block's review page renders it under
    body.path-blocks-lp.

    Kept from core: the wrapper's data-region="competencies-to-review", a table with a head and a body, the three
    column headings, one row per item with its link, the competency name triple-stashed and the person and
    the status double-stashed.
    Changed: the table is the theme's (dim-comp-table) and the review status is a status pill.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * competencies - array of competency (shortname), user (fullname), usercompetency (url, statusname)

    Example context (json):
    {
        "competencies": [
            {
                "competency": {"shortname": "Communicate clearly"}, "user": {"fullname": "Sam Student"}, "usercompetency": {"url": "https://example.com/admin/tool/lp/user_competency.php?id=7", "statusname": "Waiting for review"}
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<div data-region="competencies-to-review">
<table class="table generaltable dim-comp-table">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col">{{#str}}shortname, tool_lp{{/str}}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{#str}}user{{/str}}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{#str}}reviewstatus, tool_lp{{/str}}</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {{#competencies}}
        <tr>
            <td><a href="{{usercompetency.url}}">{{{competency.shortname}}}</a></td>
            <td>{{user.fullname}}</td>
            <td><span class="dim-comp-pill dim-comp-pill--status">{{usercompetency.statusname}}</span></td>
        </tr>
        {{/competencies}}
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
